Complete flow yaad rakho
-------------------------
main() → SpringApplication.run() → Environment → ApplicationContext → Component Scan + Auto-Configuration
→ Bean Creation + Dependency Injection → Embedded Server → Application Ready
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 1. main() method execute hota hai
    Jab application start karte ho, sabse pehle main() execute hota hai aur SpringApplication.run() call hota hai.

Step 2. @SpringBootApplication process hota hai
    - @SpringBootConfiguration
    - @EnableAutoConfiguration
    - @ComponentScan

Step 3. Environment prepare hota hai
    Spring Boot application ki configuration read karta hai, jaise:
        - application.properties ya application.yml
        - Active profiles, jaise dev, test, prod
        - Environment variables aur command-line arguments
    Isse application ki configuration available hoti hai.

Step 4. ApplicationContext create hota hai
    Spring Boot appropriate IoC container create karta hai.
    Ye container beans ko manage karega, unki dependencies inject karega aur lifecycle handle karega.

Step 5. @ComponentScan execute hota hai
    jis jis class pe @component ya stereo annotation hai unko scan krta hai

Step 6. @EnableAutoConfiguration execute hota hai
    @EnableAutoConfiguration automatically configures suitable Spring components such as DataSource, JPA,
    caching and web infrastructure based on the dependencies present on the classpath, application properties,
    existing beans and conditional rules. We can override the default configuration when required.

Step 7. Bean instances create aur dependencies inject hoti hain

Step 8. Embedded server start hota hai

Step 9. Application ready ho jaati hai